* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13g2-lock-detector-window (issue #81, Part of #16 via #78)
* Single-device AC extraction of ONE cap_cmim instance, at the geometry the
* caller substitutes. Two geometries are extracted by ../testbench/run.sh --
* the same two instance sites the SG13CMOS5L sibling record swept, ported to
* this PDK's own capacitor device:
*
*   lock_detector.XCW        w=6u l=6u m=1   -- the integrating-node cap
*   lock_detector.XDW.XC1    w=4u l=4u m=1   -- the comparator-window cap
*                                               (inside delaywin_hv)
*
* WHY THIS DECK LOOKS DIFFERENT FROM THE SG13CMOS5L SIBLING (issue #81 Scope
* item 2). SG13G2 does not use `cap_cmomi` (SG13CMOS5L's interdigitated MOM
* cap, an OSDI compact model) -- this design's netlist uses `cap_cmim`, a
* plain SPICE .subckt (capacitors_mod.lib) with NO OSDI object at all. Two
* consequences, both checked directly against the installed ihp-sg13g2 tree
* before writing this deck:
*
*   1. `cap_cmim` has a REAL characterised process corner
*      (cornerCAP.lib: cap_typ / cap_bcs / cap_wcs, +/-10% area+perimeter
*      scaling) and a genuine TNOM=27 temperature coefficient (TC1=3.6e-6,
*      TC2=2e-9 on the `cmim_core` .model card) -- unlike `cap_cmomi`, whose
*      installed cornerCAP.lib maps every corner/mismatch/stat section to the
*      SAME nominal model (sim/README.md's own "Host requirement" section).
*      So this deck sweeps the REAL corner + temperature grid directly,
*      instead of extracting one nominal value and re-injecting a synthetic
*      +/-20% band via a separate ideal-capacitor substitution
*      (../../sg13cmos5l-lock-detector-window/testbench/mom_inject.py) --
*      that whole mechanism (mom_inject.py, cmomi_nominal.py, the --soft
*      cap_cmomi.osdi preflight branch) does not carry over here; it exists
*      only because `cap_cmomi` has no corner axis of its own to sweep.
*   2. No OSDI `osdi`-load line is needed for this device at all -- `cap_cmim`
*      resolves purely from `.lib`/`.include` text, so there is no
*      host-architecture risk (sim/PORTING-osdi-host-arch.md) for this
*      instance the way there was for `cap_cmomi`'s prebuilt x86-64 ELF.
*
* Template placeholders (substituted by ../testbench/run.sh, not meant to be
* run directly): @CAP_CORNER@ (cap_typ|cap_bcs|cap_wcs, cornerCAP.lib), @W@,
* @L@, @M@ (device geometry), @TEMP@ (degC), @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (resolved
* filesystem path -- ngspice's `.lib`/`.include` parser does not expand
* shell/OS environment variables).

* cornerCAP.lib's own .LIB block already `.include`s capacitors_mod.lib (the
* file that defines the cap_cmim subckt) -- a second .include here redefines
* it and ngspice warns and ignores the redefinition, so only the corner-scaled
* @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib call is needed.
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib @CAP_CORNER@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

Xcap n1 0 cap_cmim w=@W@ l=@L@ m=@M@
Rbleed n1 0 1e14
Iac n1 0 dc 0 ac 1

.control
* 10 kHz-decade sweep in the flat capacitive region, same extraction range
* the SG13CMOS5L sibling record used (cmim_core is a plain linear .model C,
* so there is no frequency-flatness question here the way there was for
* cap_cmomi's RF-equivalent-circuit model -- confirmed by inspection of
* capacitors_mod.lib's cap_cmim subckt, which is a single series R + linear C).
ac dec 5 1k 100k
let cval = abs(1/(2*3.14159265*frequency*imag(v(n1))))
print cval
.endc
.end
